# TRUTH DRIFT — Stale versions, deleted boards, wrong counts
File: website/audit/truth-drift.oot

Verdict: FAIL-CLOSED. Public copy describes a repo layout that
governance deleted on 2026-09-02. Version tags on disk do not
match pulled/*.json or homepage cards.

## 1. llms.txt routes agents to deleted boards

llms.txt §6 lists 13 process boards:
START, RULES, NORTHSTAR, MOONSHOTS, ROADMAP, SHIPPED, FORMAT,
SECURITY, WORKFLOW, QUICKREF, CONSTRAINTS, STRUCTURE_EM, REDTEAM.

Governance v1.0.8 front door is ANCHOR.oo plus RULES.oot,
NORTHSTAR.oot, seven RFCs, and three practices.
The 13-board set is gone. Cross references in §8 point at
openOODA/START.oot and openOODA/SECURITY.oot. Those files
do not exist.

Floor: 2 / Thrust: 9 / Patch: 4 in the header is ooda 2.9.4 era.
The website tag is v1.2.10. This file is the public LLM manual.
It is the highest-drag lie in the repo.

## 2. pulled/*.json vs git tags (2026-09-04)

| Route | JSON tagline | Disk tag |
|-------|--------------|----------|
| openOODA | eight repos, v1.0.7 | v1.0.20, 11 repos |
| ooda | v0.2.1, 13 subcommands | v0.2.7 |
| std | v1.0.3, 173 modules | v1.0.8, thousands of .oo |
| opm | v0.8.x, 19 subcommands | v0.8.8 |
| lsp | v0.6.2, 16 methods | v0.6.12 |
| mcp | v0.5.0, 23 tools, 5 tiers | v0.6.10, 22 tools |
| oodar | v2.0.0 | v4.0.0 |
| oodac | v0.1.x | v0.2.2 |

openOODA.json omits website, packaging, and .github.
mcp.json still lists `estimate_chars`. mcp killed that tool.
mcp.json still lists get_security_threat_model and
get_redteam_methodology. Those boards were folded into
practices/. oodac.json tells users to `ooda build --target=`
via `cli/` v0.2.1+. The cli/ directory was renamed to ooda/.

pulled/ANCHOR.oo is closer to truth than root ANCHOR.oo.
Root ANCHOR.oo still says oodac is "coming soon" and lists
a `cli` route. pulled/oodac.json exists. There is no cli.json.

## 3. index.html homepage cards

Static cards: ooda, std, opm, cli, lsp, mcp.
Missing cards: oodar, oodac, packaging.
The `cli` card is the old name of ooda/.
EnvCap is drawn with a strikethrough as deprecated.
NORTHSTAR.oot §4.2 still lists EnvCap as a core token.
std card claims 173 modules. That count is stale.
mcp card claims 23 tools and 5 tiers. mcp/docs/TOOLS.oot
lists 22 tools and no five-tier table.
License badge href is github.com/openOODA/ooda/blob/main/LICENSE.
README.md claims MIT or Apache 2.0. LICENSE is MIT only.

## 4. Cache and sitemap

index.html and 404.html load `/src/main.js?v=1.2.0`.
The repo tag is v1.2.10. Browsers may keep a stale SPA.
sitemap.xml lists only `/` and `/llms.txt`. Hash routes
#ooda … #oodac are invisible to crawlers.
WORKFLOW.oot §0 names website/guide/*.oot. That directory
does not exist.

## 5. Route table residue

ROUTE_NAME_TO_ID uses ids 1,2,3,4,6,7,8,9. Id 5 is the
deleted cli route. renderRoute has a dead `else if (raw ===
"oodac")` branch after oodac is already handled. Ctrl+K and
`/` set location.hash to #search. There is no search view.
The wrapper also special-cases #registry. Both hashes render
"Not found."

## 6. Next repair (this repo)

1. Rewrite llms.txt from ANCHOR.oo + RULES.oot + NORTHSTAR.oot.
   Do not mention deleted ALLCAPS boards.
2. Refresh pulled/*.json numbers from current git tags, or
   replace JSON with .oot (file-law.oot §6).
3. Remove the cli card. Add oodar and oodac cards, or delete
   the static cards if the SPA already replaces them
   (spa-drag.oot §1).
4. Point the license badge at this repo LICENSE.
5. Bump the main.js cache query to the current tag, or drop
   the query and let Pages cache headers work.
